\[
\lambda \;=\;\frac{2\pi}{\operatorname{Re}(k_{\text{SPP}})}
\;=\;\frac{2\pi}{k_{0}\,
\operatorname{Re}\!\left[\sqrt{\frac{\varepsilon_{1}\,\widetilde\varepsilon_{2}}
{\;\varepsilon_{1}+ \widetilde\varepsilon_{2}\;}}\right] }
\qquad\bigl(k_{0}=2\pi/\lambda_{0}\bigr)
\]

For a metal with a small loss, \(\widetilde\varepsilon_{2}= \varepsilon_{21}+i\varepsilon_{22}\) with
\(\varepsilon_{22}\ll|\varepsilon_{21}|\), one expands to first order in
\(\varepsilon_{22}\).  The real part of the square‑root is then given by the loss‑free
value, so that the SPP wavelength to lowest order is

\[
\boxed{\;
\lambda \;\approx\; \lambda_{0}\,
\sqrt{\frac{\varepsilon_{1}+\varepsilon_{21}}
{\varepsilon_{1}\,\varepsilon_{21}}}\;
}
\]

Higher‑order corrections are of order \(\varepsilon_{22}^{2}\) and have been
neglected.  (The corresponding complex propagation constant is
\(k_{\text{SPP}}\approx k_{0}\sqrt{\frac{\varepsilon_{1}\varepsilon_{21}}
{\varepsilon_{1}+\varepsilon_{21}}}\bigl[1+i\,\frac{\varepsilon_{1}\varepsilon_{22}}
{2\varepsilon_{21}\,(\varepsilon_{1}+\varepsilon_{21})}\bigr]\).)

